WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:04.020
We've been wondering, what is Trump thinking
right now?

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:07.729
Is he thinking is Trump so delusional that
he really thinks he can steal the election

00:00:07.729 --> 00:00:08.729
from Joe Biden?

00:00:08.729 --> 00:00:14.600
There's a new report from NBC's Peter Alexander,
which is that Trump knows he can't win.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.029
He's putting on a show.

00:00:16.029 --> 00:00:20.330
Peter Alexander tweeting yesterday morning,
quote, Trump is very aware there is not a

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:25.500
path to victory, but he believes the 72 million
who voted for him deserve a fight.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:30.650
So he's battling as a form of theater for
them, a top White House aide tells me.

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:35.420
So I believe this understand the multilevel
scam that this is.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:38.980
First of all, Trump has Republicans running
all over the country claiming they have a

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:39.980
shot.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:41.750
Rudy's in Philadelphia, Eric Trump's.

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.720
And who the hell knows where?

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:46.990
He's got Secretary of State Mike Pompeo saying
we're going to have a second.

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:52.300
Trump administration press secretary Kayleigh
McEnany saying, you know, this is all it's

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:53.739
all fraud.

00:00:53.739 --> 00:00:57.360
Is this all an act where everyone knows it's
fake or does.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:00.690
Trump think it's fake, but all of his sycophants
believe it's real.

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:06.040
I don't know next layer of the scam, Trump
is raising money on this.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:12.840
So even if Trump believes this is all theater
in terms of winning, Trump is really raising

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.390
real people's money for recounts and for legal
challenges.

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:23.820
And that's the scam because the fine print
of Trump's election fraud fundraising is that

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:27.660
50 percent of the money you give goes not
to lawsuits and recounts.

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:32.590
50 percent of the money you give goes to paying
off Trump's campaign debt.

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:38.380
There are many Trump supporters, many on fixed
incomes, many with low incomes, who really

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:41.259
can't afford to be giving Trump money.

00:01:41.259 --> 00:01:45.010
And this is not nanny state stuff where I
think someone should protect them.

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:46.800
The president is scamming them.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:49.110
It's just the president shouldn't be scamming
them.

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:51.220
That said, it's not about regulation.

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:57.220
If Trump knows he can't win and he realizes
that this is theater, he's raising millions

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:02.549
of dollars from people who potentially can't
afford to be donating to Trump, who are donating

00:02:02.549 --> 00:02:04.689
because they think it might help him win.

00:02:04.689 --> 00:02:10.799
And Trump himself, according to Peter Alexander,
doesn't think this is going to make a difference.

00:02:10.799 --> 00:02:14.340
He's scamming people to pay off his campaign
debt.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:19.049
Now, I know you know, a fool and their money
are soon parted and all of that stuff.

00:02:19.049 --> 00:02:22.769
But there are more and more aides coming forward
now and saying there is not even really the

00:02:22.769 --> 00:02:24.469
idea of a plan here.

00:02:24.469 --> 00:02:30.349
This is a straight up scam. Trump aides and
advisers and allies have said there's no grand

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:31.519
strategy here.

00:02:31.519 --> 00:02:34.079
He'll file a lawsuit, he'll send a tweet,
whatever.

00:02:34.079 --> 00:02:35.699
There's no strategy.

00:02:35.699 --> 00:02:41.049
And according to The Washington Post, quote,
Asked about Trump's ultimate plan, one senior

00:02:41.049 --> 00:02:44.260
administration official chuckled and said,
you're giving everyone too much credit right

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:45.260
now.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:47.249
They're just lying to people they know.

00:02:47.249 --> 00:02:49.099
They're lying to people and they don't care.

00:02:49.099 --> 00:02:53.209
And it's not just that they're hurting people
by taking their money.

00:02:53.209 --> 00:02:55.510
They're also hurting the United States.

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:57.159
They're hurting our election process.

00:02:57.159 --> 00:02:59.089
They're hurting our democracy.

00:02:59.089 --> 00:03:03.349
And along the way, he continues to make the
United States a laughing stock.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:06.529
And he is very clearly I mean, it's a commitment
at this point.

00:03:06.529 --> 00:03:12.480
Donald Trump is committed to making the United
States a global laughingstock, not, I would

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:18.029
argue, not just until January 20th when Joe
Biden becomes president, but probably well

00:03:18.029 --> 00:03:19.540
beyond that.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:26.309
And it is all of our, you know, going back
to 2015, 2016, all of our worst fears about

00:03:26.309 --> 00:03:33.620
Donald Trump, all of our concerns about how
wacky he might be as president, how disastrous

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:35.599
they were, understated.

00:03:35.599 --> 00:03:42.209
We've talked before about this bogus term
Trump derangement syndrome used to dismiss

00:03:42.209 --> 00:03:47.049
criticism of the president saying, oh, you
people are so hyperbolic.

00:03:47.049 --> 00:03:52.790
Almost no one was hyperbolic enough about
the presidency of Donald Trump.

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:54.170
That's the reality.

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:57.169
It's starting to wrap up and that's a very
good thing.

00:03:57.169 --> 00:04:03.180
A little bit later today, I am going to talk
about what can Joe Biden get done if he doesn't

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:07.869
get the Senate, will Trump really run again
in twenty, twenty four?

00:04:07.869 --> 00:04:09.449
What's next for the Republican Party?

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:13.090
A lot of very important questions we will
deal with later.

00:04:13.090 --> 00:04:14.650
I'm glad you're here.

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:17.829
Follow me on Twitter at David Pakman.

00:04:17.829 --> 00:05:50.319
And we will be back right after this.

